        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you boondock at all, a LiFePO4 house battery is worth it. It doubles your usable power, halves the weight on the tongue and costs far less per cycle than any AGM. Battle Born is the safest buy for owners who want proven hardware and real support; SOK and Epoch give you heating and Bluetooth for less; LiTime and Redodo are the smart budget choices for warm-weather camping.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Pick the battery last. Work out your daily amp-hours, decide whether you charge below freezing, and check your converter and alternator charging before you order. Get those three right and almost any battery on this list will run your RV happily for a decade.
          </p>
